From 234502a6e1d2d149a7baeffafa172f41eed54bad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: duncan0k <dev@ark0.si>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 08:45:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 099/105] policy: relay spends of leaf version 0xe2 once
 active, and check them again when a tripwire goes

Like SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_TRIPWIRE, SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_LATTICE_TRIPWIRE becomes
a mandatory, and so a standard, script verification flag, which the
mempool drops while the next block is below the height of the lattice
tripwire rules: until then a spend of a P2MR leaf of version 0xe2 at depth
one or more is the spend of an unknown leaf version, which
DISCOURAGE_UPGRADABLE_TAPROOT_VERSION refuses, with -acceptnonstdtxn too,
so no coins go into such a leaf through the mempool before its height.
From that height the mempool adds SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_MLDSA_DISABLED for the
next block in PolicyScriptChecks and ConsensusScriptChecks, as it adds
SCRIPT_VERIFY_P2MR_EC_DISABLED, from the confirmed UTXO set.

The two tripwires share the recheck of the mempool. Elliptic curve checks
in leaf version 0xe2 follow the tripwire of leaf version 0xe0, so the
recheck now looks at the spends of both leaf versions, under the flags of
the next block, which carry both states:

- On a block connected without a reorganization, the states before the
  block are recorded, and once the coins, removeForBlock and the tip are
  this block's, the spends are checked again if either state turned from
  enabled to disabled; once, not once per state.
- During a reorganization ConnectTip checks nothing, and
  MaybeUpdateMempoolForReorg, after it has put the transactions of the
  disconnected blocks back and mended the dependencies, checks the spends
  again whenever either final state is disabled.

SpendsP2MRTripwiredLeaf did two jobs. The recheck now goes through
SpendsP2MRDisablableLeaf, which matches leaf versions 0xe0 and 0xe2; the
removal of spends through leaf version 0xe0 when a reorganization goes
back below the height of the tripwire rules keeps
SpendsP2MRTripwiredLeaf, 0xe0 only; and a new filter by the new
deployment, SpendsP2MRLatticeTripwiredLeaf, removes the spends through
leaf version 0xe2 at depth one or more, with their descendants, when one
goes back below the height of the lattice tripwire rules, whatever the
leaf holds, so on a node with -acceptnonstdtxn=1 too. The rescue lane's
rules of the mempool do not use the old function and are unchanged: its
template R1 is of leaf version 0xe0 only, and the annex of a rescue spend
through a leaf of version 0xe2 is not standard, so such a spend is valid
in a block but not relayed. The removals below the heights of
OP_CHECKMLDSA44 and OP_CHECKSLHDSA128S still look at leaf versions 0xc0
and 0xe0 only: leaf version 0xe2 executes from a height at or above both,
which the chain parameters and their options assert.

IsWitnessStandard treats leaf version 0xe2 as 0xc0 and 0xe0, at every
height, with the 80-byte limit on the stack elements and the exceptions of
templates S1 and SLH1. Template S2, ML-DSA-44 AND Schnorr in one leaf, is
not standard in leaf version 0xe2: either tripwire makes it unspendable.
